    <article class="prose-doc min-w-0">

      <section id="acceptance">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">1. Acceptance of terms</h2>
        <p>
          By accessing or using the COCOCE marketplace ("COCOCE", "the Platform", "we", "us"),
          you agree to be bound by these Terms &amp; Conditions ("Terms"). If you do not agree
          to these Terms, you must not use the Platform.
        </p>
        <p>
          These Terms apply to all visitors, registered users, vendors, and buyers. By
          registering an account, listing a product, or completing a purchase, you confirm
          that you have read, understood, and accepted these Terms in full.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="definitions" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">2. Definitions</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Platform</strong> — the COCOCE website, mobile experiences, APIs, and any related services.</li>
          <li><strong>Vendor</strong> — a registered business or individual listing products for sale on the Platform.</li>
          <li><strong>Buyer</strong> — a registered user purchasing products through the Platform.</li>
          <li><strong>Store</strong> — a vendor-operated selling presence on the Platform.</li>
          <li><strong>Listing</strong> — a vendor's offer of a specific product variant, including price and terms.</li>
          <li><strong>Catalog</strong> — the shared registry of marketplace products, families, brands, and attributes.</li>
          <li><strong>Content</strong> — text, images, videos, descriptions, and other materials uploaded to the Platform.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="eligibility" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">3. Eligibility</h2>
        <p>To use the Platform you must:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Be at least 18 years of age, or the age of legal majority in your jurisdiction;</li>
          <li>Have the legal capacity to enter into binding contracts;</li>
          <li>Not be barred from using the Platform under the laws of Rwanda or your local jurisdiction;</li>
          <li>Provide accurate, current, and complete information during registration.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Vendors must additionally be legally entitled to sell the products they list and
          must comply with all applicable business registration, tax, and consumer-protection
          laws in Rwanda.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="accounts" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">4. Accounts</h2>
        <p>
          You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your account credentials
          and for all activity that occurs under your account. You agree to:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Provide accurate registration information and keep it up to date;</li>
          <li>Notify COCOCE immediately of any unauthorised use of your account;</li>
          <li>Not share your account or transfer it to another person without our written consent;</li>
          <li>Use a strong, unique password and enable available security features.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          COCOCE is not liable for losses arising from your failure to safeguard your account.
          We may suspend or terminate accounts that we reasonably believe have been compromised
          or used in violation of these Terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="marketplace" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">5. Marketplace role</h2>
        <p>
          COCOCE operates as a <strong>marketplace</strong> that connects vendors and buyers.
          Unless expressly stated otherwise, COCOCE is not the seller of products listed on
          the Platform and is not a party to the transaction between vendor and buyer.
        </p>
        <p>
          The contract of sale is formed directly between the vendor and the buyer. Vendors
          are solely responsible for the products they list, the accuracy of their listings,
          order fulfilment, and after-sales service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="vendors" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">6. Vendor obligations</h2>
        <p>As a vendor on COCOCE, you agree to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Provide truthful, accurate, and complete information about your business and products;</li>
          <li>List only products you are legally entitled to sell and that comply with applicable law;</li>
          <li>Maintain sufficient stock or fulfilment capability for the listings you publish;</li>
          <li>Honour the prices, availability, and terms displayed at the time of purchase;</li>
          <li>Respond to buyer enquiries and disputes in a timely, professional manner;</li>
          <li>Comply with all applicable tax obligations, including VAT and income tax;</li>
          <li>Not misuse the shared catalog by creating duplicate or misleading entries;</li>
          <li>Keep your store, listings, and prices current and accurate.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Repeated failures to meet these obligations may result in listing removal, store
          suspension, or permanent removal from the Platform.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="buyers" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">7. Buyer obligations</h2>
        <p>As a buyer on COCOCE, you agree to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Provide accurate delivery and contact information;</li>
          <li>Pay for products you order in accordance with the vendor's terms;</li>
          <li>Not misuse return, refund, or dispute mechanisms;</li>
          <li>Not engage in fraudulent, abusive, or unlawful conduct on the Platform.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="catalog" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">8. Product catalog</h2>
        <p>
          Products, families, brands, and attributes on COCOCE form a <strong>shared catalog</strong>
          used by all vendors. New catalog entities may require review and verification before
          they become publicly available.
        </p>
        <p>
          Vendors may propose new products, brands, families, and attributes, but the decision
          to approve, modify, disable, or remove catalog entries rests with COCOCE. Once
          published, catalog entries are governed by the
          <a href="/docs/attribute-registry">Catalog Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="prohibited" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">9. Prohibited items and conduct</h2>
        <p>The following are strictly prohibited on the Platform:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Counterfeit, stolen, or illegally obtained goods;</li>
          <li>Weapons, controlled substances, and items restricted by Rwandan law;</li>
          <li>Products that infringe third-party intellectual property rights;</li>
          <li>Misleading, deceptive, or fraudulent listings;</li>
          <li>Content that is defamatory, obscene, or unlawful;</li>
          <li>Manipulation of prices, reviews, or search rankings;</li>
          <li>Scraping, reverse-engineering, or automated abuse of the Platform;</li>
          <li>Attempting to circumvent Platform fees or payment systems.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Violation of this section may result in immediate account termination and, where
          appropriate, referral to law-enforcement authorities.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="payments" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">10. Payments and fees</h2>
        <p>
          Buyers pay for products through the payment methods made available on the Platform.
          Vendors receive payouts according to the settlement schedule communicated to them.
        </p>
        <p>
          COCOCE may charge commissions, listing fees, or other charges. Applicable fees are
          disclosed to vendors before they are incurred and may be updated with reasonable
          notice. Vendors are responsible for any taxes applicable to their sales.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="shipping" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">11. Shipping and delivery</h2>
        <p>
          Shipping methods, delivery estimates, and shipping costs are set by each vendor and
          displayed on the relevant listing. Vendors are responsible for dispatching products
          accurately and on time, and for providing tracking information where available.
        </p>
        <p>
          Risk of loss passes in accordance with applicable consumer-protection law and the
          vendor's stated shipping terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="returns" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">12. Returns and refunds</h2>
        <p>
          Return and refund policies are set by each vendor and displayed on the listing.
          Buyers should review the vendor's policy before purchasing. Returns must comply with
          the vendor's stated conditions and applicable Rwandan consumer-protection law.
        </p>
        <p>
          Disputes between buyers and vendors should first be resolved directly. If a
          resolution cannot be reached, either party may contact COCOCE support for mediation.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="ip" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">13. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          The COCOCE name, logo, platform design, and underlying technology are owned by
          COCOCE and its licensors. You may not copy, modify, or redistribute them without
          written permission.
        </p>
        <p>
          Vendors retain ownership of the content they upload. By uploading content, you grant
          COCOCE a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free licence to display, reproduce, and
          distribute that content on the Platform and in connection with its normal operation.
        </p>
        <p>
          You represent that you have the rights necessary to upload any content you submit
          and that doing so does not infringe the rights of any third party.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="liability" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">14. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by law, COCOCE shall not be liable for any indirect,
          incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages arising out of or relating
          to your use of the Platform, including lost profits, lost revenue, or lost data.
        </p>
        <p>
          COCOCE's total aggregate liability for any claim arising from these Terms or your
          use of the Platform shall not exceed the greater of (a) the amount of fees you paid
          to COCOCE in the twelve months preceding the claim, or (b) RWF 100,000.
        </p>
        <p>
          Nothing in these Terms excludes liability that cannot be excluded under applicable
          law, including liability for fraud or wilful misconduct.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="termination" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">15. Suspension and termination</h2>
        <p>
          COCOCE may suspend or terminate your access to the Platform at any time, with or
          without notice, if we reasonably believe you have breached these Terms, engaged in
          fraudulent or unlawful conduct, or posed a risk to other users or to the Platform.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may close your account at any time by contacting support. Obligations that by
          their nature should survive termination — including payment obligations, intellectual
          property provisions, and limitations of liability — shall survive.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="changes" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">16. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          COCOCE may update these Terms from time to time. Material changes will be communicated
          through the Platform or by email before they take effect. Continued use of the
          Platform after changes take effect constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms.
        </p>
        <p>
          The "Last updated" date at the top of this page reflects the most recent revision.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="law" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">17. Governing law and disputes</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Rwanda. Any dispute arising
          out of or in connection with these Terms shall be subject to the exclusive
          jurisdiction of the courts of Kigali, Rwanda, unless mandatory consumer-protection
          law provides otherwise.
        </p>
        <p>
          Before commencing formal proceedings, the parties agree to attempt to resolve any
          dispute in good faith through COCOCE's support and mediation channels.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="contact" class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-3">18. Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about these Terms may be sent to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>General support — <a href="mailto:support@cococe.rw">sales@cococe.rw</a></li>
          <li>Legal enquiries — <a href="mailto:legal@cococe.rw">sales@cococe.rw</a></li>
          <li>Privacy matters — <a href="mailto:privacy@cococe.rw">sales@cococe.rw</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12 pt-6 border-t border-ink-200">
        <p class="text-xs text-ink-400">
          This document is provided for informational purposes and does not constitute legal
          advice. COCOCE recommends that vendors and buyers seek independent legal advice
          where appropriate. If anything here conflicts with mandatory law, the law prevails.
        </p>
      </section>

